📘 Analysis of Algorithms — Complete Master Notes
1. Introduction to Analysis of Algorithms

Analysis of Algorithms computer science का fundamental topic है जिसमें algorithms की performance और efficiency evaluate की जाती है।

Efficiency को दो मुख्य factors से measure किया जाता है:

Time Complexity → Algorithm को run होने में कितना समय लगता है

Space Complexity → Algorithm को कितनी memory चाहिए

Example

अगर दो algorithms same problem solve करते हैं:

Algorithm A → 1 second

Algorithm B → 5 seconds

तो Algorithm A ज्यादा efficient है।

2. Why Analysis of Algorithms is Important

Software design में कई चीजें important होती हैं:

User-friendliness

Security

Maintainability

Modularity

लेकिन इन सबको achieve करने के लिए performance जरूरी है.

Algorithm analysis के main goals

Large input behavior predict करना

Algorithms compare करना

Efficient algorithm choose करना

Hardware independent analysis करना

Example
Binary Search vs Linear Search

Linear search → O(n)

Binary search → O(log n)

Large data में binary search ज्यादा efficient है.

3. Order of Growth

Order of growth बताता है कि input size बढ़ने पर algorithm का time कैसे बढ़ेगा.

Example

f(n) = 1000
g(n) = n + 1

n बड़ा होने पर g(n) तेजी से बढ़ेगा।

Order of Growth निकालने का rule

Lower order terms ignore करो

Constants ignore करो

Example

f(n) = 4n² + 3n + 100

Steps:

Lower terms remove → 4n²
Constant remove → n²

✔ Order of growth = n²

Growth Comparison

c < log log n < log n < √n < n < n log n < n² < n³ < 2ⁿ < n!

4. Asymptotic Analysis

Asymptotic analysis algorithm performance को input size के basis पर analyze करता है.

इसमें machine speed ignore की जाती है।

Example

Search problem

Algorithms:

Linear Search

Binary Search

Small inputs पर linear search fast हो सकता है
लेकिन large inputs पर binary search better हो जाता है.

Advantages

Machine independent analysis

Large inputs के लिए accurate

Limitations

Constant factors ignore करता है

Small inputs के लिए हमेशा accurate नहीं

5. Worst Case, Average Case, Best Case
Worst Case

Maximum time required.

Example
Linear search में element list में नहीं हो.

✔ Most commonly used analysis

Best Case

Minimum time required.

Example
Element first position पर हो.

✔ Rarely used.

Average Case

Average time across all inputs.

✔ Difficult to calculate.

6. Time Complexity

Time complexity बताती है algorithm कितनी operations perform करता है.

Example
Loop n times run करे → O(n)

Time complexity measure करने के लिए primitive operations count किए जाते हैं.

7. Common Time Complexity Classes
Complexity	Meaning	Example
O(1)	Constant	Print statement
O(log n)	Logarithmic	Binary search
O(n)	Linear	Linear search
O(n log n)	Superlinear	Merge sort
O(n²)	Quadratic	Bubble sort
O(n³)	Cubic	Matrix multiplication
O(2ⁿ)	Exponential	Tower of Hanoi
O(n!)	Factorial	Permutations

Algorithms का runtime input size के साथ rapidly बढ़ सकता है.

8. Big-O Notation

Big-O notation algorithm का upper bound बताता है.

Definition:

f(n) = O(g(n))

अगर

f(n) ≤ C × g(n)

for n ≥ n₀

तो f(n) = O(g(n))

Big-O निकालने का quick rule

Highest order term लो

Constant remove करो

Example

f(n) = 3n² + 2n + 100

✔ Big-O = O(n²)

Big-O Properties

Reflexivity

Transitivity

Symmetry (कुछ cases में)

9. Big Omega (Ω) Notation

Big Omega algorithm का lower bound बताता है.

Definition

f(n) ≥ C × g(n)

Example

Best case time of linear search → Ω(1)

10. Big Theta (Θ) Notation

Theta notation exact bound बताती है.

Definition

C1 g(n) ≤ f(n) ≤ C2 g(n)

Example

Merge sort

Θ(n log n)

11. Space Complexity

Space complexity algorithm की memory usage बताती है.

Types

Input space

Auxiliary space

Example

Array size n → O(n)
Matrix n×n → O(n²)

12. Analysis of Loops
Single Loop
for(i=1;i<=n;i++)

Time complexity

O(n)

Nested Loop
for(i=1;i<=n;i++)
 for(j=1;j<=n;j++)

Time complexity

O(n²)

Logarithmic Loop
for(i=1;i<n;i*=2)

Time complexity

O(log n)

Consecutive loops

Time complexity add होती है.

Example

O(n) + O(m) = O(n+m)

13. Recursive Algorithm Analysis

Recursive algorithm में time complexity recurrence relation से मिलती है.

Example

Merge sort

T(n) = 2T(n/2) + cn

Recurrence solve करने के methods

Substitution Method

Recurrence Tree

Master Theorem

Example

T(n) = 3T(n-1)

Solve करने पर

T(n) = 3ⁿ

14. Amortized Analysis

Amortized analysis operations की average cost over sequence analyze करता है.

Example

Dynamic array insertion

Most insertions → O(1)
Resizing → O(n)

लेकिन amortized cost

✔ O(1)

Techniques

Aggregate Method

Accounting Method

Potential Method

15. Example: Dynamic Array Resizing

Steps

Array full हो जाए

नया array allocate करो

Data copy करो

Old array delete करो

Worst case → O(n)

लेकिन amortized insertion

✔ O(1)

16. Amortized Analysis Example (Red-Black Tree)

Potential function φ define करते हैं:

g(n) values assign करके tree की potential calculate होती है.

Amortized cost formula

Amortized cost = actual cost + change in potential

17. Complexity Classes

Computational problems को classes में divide किया जाता है.

Purpose

Efficient problems identify करना

Hard problems classify करना

18. P Class

Polynomial time में solve होने वाले problems.

Time complexity

O(nᵏ)

Examples

Merge sort

GCD

Maximum matching

✔ Efficient problems

19. NP Class

NP = Non-deterministic Polynomial Time

Properties

Solution verify करना easy

Solution find करना difficult

Example

SAT problem

Graph coloring

Hamiltonian path

20. Co-NP Class

NP problems का complement.

Meaning

अगर answer NO है
तो proof verify किया जा सकता है.

Example

Prime number checking

21. NP-Hard Problems

NP-Hard problems:

NP से भी difficult

Polynomial solution नहीं पता

Examples

Traveling Salesman Problem

22. NP-Complete Problems

NP-Complete problems:

NP में होते हैं

NP-Hard भी होते हैं

Example

SAT problem

अगर किसी NP-complete problem का polynomial solution मिल जाए

✔ सभी NP problems solve हो सकती हैं.

⭐ Final Summary

Analysis of Algorithms में मुख्य concepts:

Algorithm performance evaluation

Time complexity

Space complexity

Asymptotic analysis

Big-O, Ω, Θ notations

Loop analysis

Recursion analysis

Amortized analysis

Complexity classes (P, NP, NP-Complete)